<title>USA: Duquesne Pa. nukes seen down 7-10 days.</title>
<headline>Duquesne Pa. nukes seen down 7-10 days.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dusquesne Light Co said Thursday both of its Beaver Valley nuclear units would likely remain off-line for seven to 10 days after tripping off line late Wednesday.</p>
<p>The cause of the shutdown was still not yet known, a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Unit 1, with a rated capacity of 810 megawatts (MW), and unit 2, rated at 833 MW, are both located in Shippingport, Pa.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
